      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why are the -\u003esetup_rq_keyslot_manager() and -\u003edestroy_keyslot_manager() Android-specific variant ops needed?  Everyone should be using hba-\u003eksm, right?  They might initialize it as a \"passthrough\" keyslot manager, but they will still be using it.  So why not just remove these variant ops and use the code directly from v9:\n\nvoid ufshcd_crypto_setup_rq_keyslot_manager(struct ufs_hba *hba,\n                                            struct request_queue *q)\n{\n        if ((hba-\u003ecaps \u0026 UFSHCD_CAP_CRYPTO))\n                blk_ksm_register(\u0026hba-\u003eksm, q);\n}\n\nvoid ufshcd_crypto_destroy_keyslot_manager(struct ufs_hba *hba)\n{\n        blk_ksm_destroy(\u0026hba-\u003eksm);\n}",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 275,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 275,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "3f3ac530c9fe675b12905f4d6e1985603d1c0c0e",
